    "proof": "Grouping equal exponents gives E=sum h_a b^(-a). Multiplication by b^U produces an integer whose base-b digit at place U-a is h_a. No carry occurs because h_a<=B=b-1, and uniqueness of finite radix expansions proves exact recovery. The pairs [1,M] and [1,M+1] have different histograms but selector distance (b-1)/b^(M+1), so uniform fixed absolute precision cannot recover arbitrarily deep histogram digits.",
    "radix_identity": "b^U E=sum_a h_a b^(U-a), b=B+1",
